{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _has_zero_sum_triple(nums: list) -> bool:\n        # Sort the list to efficiently find triples and manage duplicates.\n        # This approach provides O(N^2) time complexity after sorting.\n        nums.sort()\n        n = len(nums)\n\n        for i in range(n - 2):\n            # Skip duplicate elements for the first number (a) to avoid duplicate triplets\n            # and ensure selected 'a' is a distinct value from previous iterations.\n            if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i-1]:\n                continue\n\n            # Use two pointers, 'left' and 'right', for the remaining part of the array\n            # to find two other distinct elements (b and c) that sum to -nums[i].\n            left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n            while left < right:\n                current_sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right]\n\n                if current_sum == 0:\n                    # Found a triplet (nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]).\n                    # Due to sorting and duplicate skipping, these three numbers\n                    # are guaranteed to be distinct values.\n                    return True\n                elif current_sum < 0:\n                    # Sum is too small, increment 'left' pointer to increase the sum.\n                    left += 1\n                else: # current_sum > 0\n                    # Sum is too large, decrement 'right' pointer to decrease the sum.\n                    right -= 1\n                    \n        return False\n\n    # FR3: Return False for lists with fewer than three elements.\n    if len(l) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # FR4: Preserve Input List - create a copy for the helper function to sort.\n    l_copy = list(l)\n\n    # Delegate the core logic to the private helper function.\n    return _has_zero_sum_triple(l_copy)"}
