{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    is_negative = x < 0\n    n = abs(x)\n    digits = []\n\n    while n > 0:\n        digits.append(str(n % base))\n        n //= base\n\n    if not digits:  # Handles the case where x was 0\n        return '0'\n\n    if is_negative:\n        digits.append('-')\n\n    return ''.join(reversed(digits))"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence efficiently without recursion.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the base values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    # a = fib4(i-4), b = fib4(i-3), c = fib4(i-2), d = fib4(i-1)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from i = 4 up to n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift values for the next iteration\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_fib\n    \n    return d"}
